I built the workflow and saved it as slot w4-C-b1. It starts a call, but its first sentence doesn't match the brief word for word.

- **Checks:** The lint check and the situations check both report no problems. One live chat turn worked.
- **Opening wording:** The brief requires "Hello, this is the virtual assistant of FB Services. This call is recorded." In the live turn the agent said "…FB Services; we record this call." My file has the exact sentence, so the change probably happens when the platform or the save step converts the opening. I ran out of time to fix it.
- **Structure:** The date code node is the start node. The `get_account` lookup and its hook sit between identity and a router, which hands off to the main negotiation node. Each of the six exit situations (refused, over_limit, hardship, dispute, already_paid, transfer) has its own node. Every node that can close sends the call to a final hang-up node once `close_call` succeeds.
- **Rules I added to the account hook:** The tested hook code is unchanged. After it I added code for two rules the code steps don't compute:
  - **Deadline for 1,000.00 or more:** credit cards and personal loans with arrears of 1,000.00 or more get a 7-day deadline, moved back to a business day.
  - **Two-part plan amounts:** each account gets its two halves, with the extra cent on part 1.

  The extracted situations matched the brief, so I didn't change any.
- **Goodbye said once:** The brief says the agent speaks "Thank you for your time. Goodbye." before `close_call`. So I made the hang-up node silent, so the goodbye isn't said twice.
- **Wrong-answer counting not confirmed:** The identity step counts a wrong answer when the result has `correct: false` or a similar flag. The API file doesn't say which field the verify result uses, so this is unconfirmed.

